   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Money in and money out",
     "texto": [
      "**The account.** You open a **cuenta corriente**. They **ingresan** your salary, you **retiras** money at the cash machine and make a **transferencia** to pay someone. What is left is **el saldo**. If it is negative, you are **en números rojos**. The bank charges **comisiones**.\n\n**Bills.** You can **domiciliar** the electricity bill: the bank pays it by itself.\n\n**Borrowing.** You ask for a loan and the bank **concede** it or denies it. You pay it back in **plazos**, with a fixed or variable **tipo de interés**.\n\n**Plazo** has three meanings: a payment (**a plazos**), a period (**a largo plazo**) and a deadline (**el plazo termina** tomorrow).\n\n**Investing.** You **inviertes** to make **ganancias**, but you can also have losses.\n\n**Taxes.** Each year you do the **declaración de la renta**. It comes out **a pagar** or **a devolver**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Plazo, percentages and «salir a pagar»",
     "texto": [
      "**Plazo** has three meanings: a payment (**pagar a plazos**), a period (**a corto plazo**, **a largo plazo**) and a deadline (**el plazo termina el treinta**).\n\n**Percentages take an article**: **un tres por ciento**, **el veinte por ciento de los clientes**.\n\n**Salir a pagar / a devolver** gives the result of the tax return: **me sale a pagar**, **me sale a devolver**. The **me** is the person affected.\n\n**Ingresar** money **en** the account and **retirar** money **del** cash machine are opposite verbs."
     ],
